---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HeroSection from '../components/HeroSection.astro';
import CTAButton from '../components/CTAButton.astro';
import { Minus, Check, Shield, Zap, RefreshCw, Heart, Sparkles, ChevronRight } from '@lucide/astro';
import FAQSection from '../components/FAQSection.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="IV Vitamin C Therapy in Halifax"
  description="IV vitamin C therapy in Halifax with individual assessment, screening, informed consent and a balanced discussion of evidence and risks."
  focusKeyword="IV vitamin C Halifax"
>
  <HeroSection
    title="IV Vitamin C Therapy"
    compact
    image={{ src: "/images/services/iv-therapy.webp", alt: "IV vitamin C therapy", aspect: "video" }}
  >
    <p>Intravenous vitamin C produces different blood concentrations than oral vitamin C, but that pharmacological difference does not establish benefit for every symptom or condition. Assessment, screening and informed consent come first.</p>
    <CTAButton slot="cta">Book Online</CTAButton>
  </HeroSection>

  <!-- Key Benefits -->
  <section class="py-12 bg-white">
    <div class="section-shell">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-8 text-center">
        <div>
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-700 mb-2">Direct</div>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">intravenous administration</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-700 mb-2">Individual</div>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">indication and formulation review</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="text-4xl font-bold text-emerald-700 mb-2">45-90</div>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">minutes per treatment session</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-700 mb-2">Screened</div>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">for contraindications and risks</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why IV vs Oral -->
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-24 bg-emerald-50">
    <div class="section-shell">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-serif font-medium text-emerald-950 mb-6">IV and Oral Vitamin C Are Different</h2>
        <div class="prose prose-lg text-slate-600 mb-8">
          <p>
            Oral absorption is regulated by the gastrointestinal tract, and the fraction absorbed decreases as oral doses increase. Higher oral intake can also cause digestive effects.
          </p>
          <p>
            IV administration bypasses gastrointestinal absorption and produces higher circulating concentrations. Higher concentration is a pharmacological fact, not proof of a better clinical outcome. The relevance depends on the indication and supporting evidence.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
          <div class="site-card-interactive p-8">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-xl text-emerald-950 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="w-8 h-8 bg-slate-200 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-slate-600 text-sm font-bold">C</span>
              Oral Vitamin C
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-600">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <Minus class="w-5 h-5 text-slate-400 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>Absorption is regulated and dose-dependent</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <Minus class="w-5 h-5 text-slate-400 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>Higher doses cause GI upset</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <Minus class="w-5 h-5 text-slate-400 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>Produces lower circulating concentrations than IV administration</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <Minus class="w-5 h-5 text-slate-400 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>Often the less invasive route when supplementation is indicated</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white border border-emerald-100 rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-xl text-emerald-950 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="w-8 h-8 bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">IV</span>
              IV Vitamin C
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-600">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <Check class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-600 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>Enters the circulation directly</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <Check class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-600 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>Bypasses GI tract entirely</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <Check class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-600 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>Produces higher circulating concentrations</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <Check class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-600 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>Clinical benefit must be established separately for each use</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What IV Vitamin C Treats -->
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-24 bg-white">
    <div class="section-shell">
      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-serif font-medium text-emerald-950 mb-4">Who Benefits from IV Vitamin C?</h2>
        <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          IV vitamin C supports multiple aspects of health through its antioxidant, immune-supporting and tissue-repair properties.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <!-- Immune Support -->
        <div class="bg-emerald-50 rounded-2xl p-6 card-hover">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-emerald-700 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <Shield class="w-6 h-6 text-white" aria-hidden="true" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-lg text-emerald-950 mb-2">Immune Function</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Vitamin C has established biological roles in immune function. This does not establish IV vitamin C as a treatment for acute infection.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Acute Illness -->
        <div class="bg-emerald-50 rounded-2xl p-6 card-hover">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-emerald-700 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <Zap class="w-6 h-6 text-white" aria-hidden="true" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-lg text-emerald-950 mb-2">Acute Illness Evidence</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Research in acute illness is condition- and setting-specific. It does not support routine IV treatment for common infections.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Post-Viral Recovery -->
        <div class="bg-emerald-50 rounded-2xl p-6 card-hover">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-emerald-700 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <RefreshCw class="w-6 h-6 text-white" aria-hidden="true" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-lg text-emerald-950 mb-2">Post-Viral Symptoms</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Evidence does not establish IV vitamin C as a treatment for Long COVID or post-viral fatigue. Persistent symptoms require appropriate assessment.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Fatigue -->
        <div class="bg-emerald-50 rounded-2xl p-6 card-hover">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-emerald-700 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <Zap class="w-6 h-6 text-white" aria-hidden="true" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-lg text-emerald-950 mb-2">Fatigue</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Fatigue has many possible causes. Limited studies do not justify presenting IV vitamin C as a general fatigue treatment.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Stress -->
        <div class="bg-emerald-50 rounded-2xl p-6 card-hover">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-emerald-700 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <Heart class="w-6 h-6 text-white" aria-hidden="true" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-lg text-emerald-950 mb-2">Stress Claims</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">The presence of vitamin C in adrenal tissue does not establish that IV vitamin C treats stress or “adrenal depletion.”</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Skin & Collagen -->
        <div class="bg-emerald-50 rounded-2xl p-6 card-hover">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-emerald-700 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <Sparkles class="w-6 h-6 text-white" aria-hidden="true" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-lg text-emerald-950 mb-2">Collagen Biology</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Vitamin C is required for normal collagen synthesis, but this does not establish high-dose IV treatment for skin or connective-tissue concerns.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Science -->
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-24 bg-emerald-950">
    <div class="section-shell">
      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-serif font-medium !text-white mb-6">The Science of IV Vitamin C</h2>
          <div class="prose prose-lg prose-invert">
            <p class="text-white/90">
              Vitamin C (ascorbic acid) is a potent antioxidant and essential cofactor for numerous enzymatic reactions in the body. It supports immune function through multiple mechanisms:
            </p>
            <ul class="text-white/90">
              <li><strong class="!text-white">Enhances neutrophil function</strong>, improving their ability to engulf and destroy pathogens</li>
              <li><strong class="!text-white">Supports T and B cell development</strong>, critical for adaptive immunity</li>
              <li><strong class="!text-white">Increases antibody production</strong>. Studies show higher IgA, IgG and IgM levels with supplementation</li>
              <li><strong class="!text-white">Reduces oxidative stress</strong>, protecting cells from damage during infection</li>
              <li><strong class="!text-white">Supports collagen synthesis</strong>, essential for tissue repair and wound healing</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-white/90">
              At high concentrations achievable only through IV administration, vitamin C may also have pro-oxidant effects that help fight certain pathogens while remaining protective to healthy cells.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white/10 backdrop-blur rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-xl text-white mb-6">How to Read the Research</h3>
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="border-b border-white/20 pb-4">
              <p class="text-white/90 text-sm mb-2">
                Biological roles of vitamin C do not by themselves demonstrate that an IV infusion improves clinical outcomes.
              </p>
              <p class="text-emerald-400 text-xs">Biological plausibility is not treatment evidence</p>
            </div>
            <div class="border-b border-white/20 pb-4">
              <p class="text-white/90 text-sm mb-2">
                Findings from one condition, dose or hospital setting should not be generalized to routine wellness or unrelated symptoms.
              </p>
              <p class="text-emerald-400 text-xs">Indication-specific evidence matters</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="text-white/90 text-sm mb-2">
                Early or exploratory findings need confirmation in adequately powered trials before being advertised as patient benefit.
              </p>
              <p class="text-emerald-400 text-xs">Study quality and endpoints matter</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Treatment Options -->
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-24 bg-white">
    <div class="section-shell">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-serif font-medium text-emerald-950 mb-6 text-center">Treatment Options</h2>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
          <!-- Myers with extra C -->
          <div class="bg-emerald-50 rounded-2xl p-8 card-hover">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-xl text-emerald-950 mb-4">Myers' Cocktail + Vitamin C</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">A Myers' Cocktail generally combines vitamin C with B vitamins, magnesium and calcium. Formulations vary, and evidence for broad wellness, fatigue or immune claims is limited.</p>
            <a href="/myers-cocktail-intravenous-nutrients/" class="text-emerald-700 text-sm font-medium mt-4 inline-flex items-center hover:text-emerald-800">
              Learn more about Myers' Cocktail
              <ChevronRight class="w-4 h-4 ml-1" aria-hidden="true" />
            </a>
          </div>

          <!-- High-dose C -->
          <div class="bg-emerald-50 rounded-2xl p-8 card-hover">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-xl text-emerald-950 mb-4">High-Dose Vitamin C</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">Higher-dose vitamin C requires a clear, evidence-informed rationale and additional screening. It is not presented as routine care for acute illness or post-viral recovery.</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-4">G6PD screening required before first high-dose treatment</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What to Expect -->
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-24 bg-emerald-50">
    <div class="section-shell">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-serif font-medium text-emerald-950 mb-8 text-center">What to Expect</h2>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="flex gap-6 items-start">
            <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-12 h-12 bg-emerald-700 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-white font-bold text-lg">1</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-xl text-emerald-950 mb-2">Initial Consultation</h3>
              <p class="text-slate-600">We'll review your health history, discuss the proposed indication and determine whether treatment is appropriate. For high-dose vitamin C, G6PD screening is required before treatment.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex gap-6 items-start">
            <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-12 h-12 bg-emerald-700 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-white font-bold text-lg">2</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-xl text-emerald-950 mb-2">During Treatment</h3>
              <p class="text-slate-600">You'll relax in a comfortable chair while the IV infuses over 30-90 minutes depending on the dose. Many people read, work on their laptop or simply rest. You may feel a mild cooling sensation or taste vitamin C during the infusion, which is normal.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex gap-6 items-start">
            <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-12 h-12 bg-emerald-700 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-white font-bold text-lg">3</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-xl text-emerald-950 mb-2">After Treatment</h3>
              <p class="text-slate-600">Most people feel energized after their infusion. You can drive and return to normal activities immediately. Stay well-hydrated for the rest of the day.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="site-card-interactive mt-12 p-8">
          <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-xl text-emerald-950 mb-4">Preparation Tips</h3>
          <ul class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-slate-600">
              <Check class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-600 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
              <span>Eat a light meal before your appointment</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-slate-600">
              <Check class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-600 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
              <span>Stay well-hydrated beforehand</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-slate-600">
              <Check class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-600 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
              <span>Wear comfortable, loose-fitting sleeves</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-slate-600">
              <Check class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-600 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" />
              <span>Bring something to read or do during infusion</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Safety -->
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-24 bg-white">
    <div class="section-shell">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-serif font-medium text-emerald-950 mb-6">Safety & Considerations</h2>

        <div class="prose prose-lg text-slate-600 mb-8">
          <p>
            IV vitamin C is an invasive treatment with formulation- and dose-dependent risks. Screening reduces risk but does not eliminate it. Important considerations include:
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
          <div class="bg-emerald-50 rounded-2xl p-6 card-hover">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-lg text-emerald-950 mb-4">G6PD Deficiency Screening</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">
              People with G6PD deficiency (a genetic enzyme deficiency) should not receive high-dose vitamin C, as it can cause red blood cell breakdown. We require a simple blood test before your first high-dose treatment to ensure safety. This is a one-time test.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-emerald-50 rounded-2xl p-6 card-hover">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-lg text-emerald-950 mb-4">Kidney Considerations</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">
              High-dose vitamin C is processed by the kidneys. If you have kidney disease or a history of kidney stones, we'll discuss whether IV vitamin C is appropriate and may adjust the protocol accordingly.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-emerald-50 rounded-2xl p-6 card-hover">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-lg text-emerald-950 mb-4">Common Side Effects</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">
              Potential effects include pain, bruising, inflammation or infection at the IV site, thirst, nausea, light-headedness, fluid or electrolyte changes and reactions to an ingredient. Serious risks vary with dose and health history.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-emerald-50 rounded-2xl p-6 card-hover">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-lg text-emerald-950 mb-4">Medication Interactions</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">
              Please inform us of all medications you're taking. Some medications may interact with high-dose vitamin C. We'll review your medications during your consultation.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FAQSection items={[
          { question: "How often is IV vitamin C given?", answer: "<p>There is no general schedule appropriate for website readers. Whether it is offered or repeated depends on a supportable indication, response, risks and alternatives. Some proposed uses do not justify treatment.</p>" },
          { question: "Can I get IV vitamin C while I'm sick?", answer: "<p>Acute symptoms should first be assessed to determine whether medical testing, isolation precautions or another form of care is needed. IV vitamin C has not been established as routine treatment for common viral infections or as a way to recover faster.</p>" },
          { question: "Is IV vitamin C the same as getting a vitamin C shot?", answer: "<p>No. Intramuscular vitamin C \"shots\" deliver a much smaller amount. IV infusion allows us to deliver significantly higher doses over time, achieving the blood concentrations needed for therapeutic effects.</p>" },
          { question: "Should I combine oral and IV vitamin C?", answer: "<p>Do not add or change supplements based on this page. Total intake, diet, kidney function, medications and the reason for treatment should be reviewed individually.</p>" },
        ]} />

  <!-- CTA Section -->
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-24 bg-emerald-950">
    <div class="section-shell">
      <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-serif font-medium text-white mb-6">Considering IV Vitamin C?</h2>
        <p class="text-lg text-white/90 mb-8">
          Book a consultation to review the proposed indication, evidence, alternatives, screening requirements and potential risks. An assessment does not mean treatment will be recommended.
        </p>
        <CTAButton source="iv-vitamin-c-cta" />
        <p class="text-white/70 mt-6 text-sm">Initial consultation required for new patients | Most extended health plans cover naturopathic services</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
